WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:06.510
From the moment we were brought here in bondage

00:00:06.510 --> 00:00:11.270
in 1619, Black life in this country
has been defined by hard work,

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:14.560
and our labor has generated
success stories

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:16.230
that deserve to be celebrated.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:24.740
Commonly, people refer to “The 1619 Project”

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:26.700
as a history, but it's not a history.

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:29.500
It really is talking about America today.

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:32.870
“The 1619 Project” is a six-part docuseries

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:36.840
that explores all aspects of American life
through the lens of slavery.

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:42.470
Each episode has its own story
arc and has its own particular beat in history.

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:45.260
We were told that by virtue
of our bondage,

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:47.390
we would never be American,

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:49.560
but it was by virtue of our bondage

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:52.350
that we became the most American of all.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:55.940
The very first episode is “Democracy,”

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:59.280
and it really talks
about how Black Americans have been

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:03.910
the primary democratizing force
over generations in this country.

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:08.530
I want to be able to look back and say,
I did this so that you didn't have to.

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:10.450
That's what legacy is all about.

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:15.500
The “Race” episode deals with the idea
that race is a construct

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:19.000
that was made up to divide
the powerful from the powerless.

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:21.550
This is a power hierarchy,

00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:24.680
whether we're talking about
where you live, what kind of job

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:28.100
you can have, and just in general
how you're valued in society.

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:30.850
The “Music” episode is about

00:01:30.850 --> 00:01:34.980
how Black music is in
every aspect of American life.

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:38.770
There's a whole cultural experience
that is fascinating and foreign

00:01:38.770 --> 00:01:39.690
to White people.

00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:41.150
They are drawn to this music.

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:44.530
The “Capitalism”
episode looks at the particular

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:47.200
brutality of the exploitation of labor.

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:52.160
I'm looking at the names of people
and their value in the slave ledgers,

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:56.870
and they're being listed
literally next to a pig or cow.

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:58.380
It's something I'll never forget.

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:02.510
The episode around fear examines
the fear of Black men

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:04.300
and how that still plays out today.

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:05.430
Jefferson was always worried

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:08.340
about the revolution
of the wheel of fortune - that is,

00:02:08.510 --> 00:02:10.600
we're on top now, but this thing can spin.

00:02:10.970 --> 00:02:15.140
The “Justice” episode makes the argument
that there is a great moral

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:18.190
and financial debt
that is owed to Black Americans.

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:20.860
You are calling for reparations.

00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:22.940
What is the total that would be owed?

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:26.490
I've seen estimates as high as $14
trillion.

00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:27.950
That's a big number.

00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:28.910
It’s a big debt, though.

00:02:28.910 --> 00:02:29.780
It is a big debt.

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:36.910
I think people are going to be compelled
and surprised and hurt

00:02:37.210 --> 00:02:41.170
but also come away with a newfound respect
for the role

00:02:41.170 --> 00:02:43.000
that Black Americans
have played in this country.

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:46.880
We are still here and we're still fighting,
as long as there’s life,

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:48.180
we're going to have hope.

00:02:50.090 --> 00:02:53.390
What if America understood after four hundred years

00:02:53.390 --> 00:02:56.310
that Black people have never been
the problem

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:57.690
but the solution?

